From 4b60fcbbcd42f67bf6fa67af213751da0b0df58f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:17:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/11] fix(#94): RemovalReport.not_found and .parametrized are
 computed from outcomes, the one record

The defect, verbatim from the issue: "a computed field no reader reads is invisible". `not_found` and
`parametrized` were stored copies of what `outcomes` (the complete per-id record the --remove page reads,
#103) already says; production read neither, and a report built with one disagreeing with the other was
possible.

Why the obvious fix is wrong: deleting them outright would orphan two test files that state a real
contract (an id kept for any reason but being a row; a bracketed row) and lose the vocabulary. They are
now properties of `outcomes`, so there is one source and the two test files keep asserting the same
behaviour unchanged.

Not closed: the other 10 OPEN fields of tests/test_field_consumption_intent.py.

OPEN 12 -> 10. Disarmed (the old stored fields), the new intent test fails (1 of 1). 191 tests in the
removal neighbours and the guards pass under 3.14 and 3.12 apart from the unrelated `bound` entry of
test_absorbed_rename_intent (the integration Wesker now declares it); ruff clean under pinned 0.16.7.
